{number: 24}
{title: Joy to the World! The Lord Is Come}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Joy to the world! the [F] Lord is [G] come:
Let [C] earth receive her [G] King;
Let [C] every [C7] heart pre-[F] pare Him room,
And [C] heaven and nature sing,
And [G] heaven and nature sing,
And [C] heaven, and [F] heaven [C] and na-[G] ture [C] sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Joy to the earth! the [F] Savior [G] reigns:
Let [C] men their songs em-[G] ploy;
While [C] fields and [C7] floods, rocks, [F] hills, and plains
Re-[C] peat the sounding joy,
Re-[G] peat the sounding joy,
Re-[C] peat, re-[F] peat, [C] the soun-[G] ding [C] joy.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] No more let sins and [F] sorrows [G] grow,
Nor [C] thorns infest the [G] ground;
He [C] comes to [C7] make His [F] blessings flow
Far [C] as the curse is found,
Far [G] as the curse is found,
Far [C] as, far [F] as, [C] the cur-[G] se is [C] found.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] He rules the world with [F] truth and [G] grace,
And [C] makes the nations [G] prove
The [C] glories [C7] of His [F] righteousness,
And [C] wonders of His love,
And [G] wonders of His love,
And [C] wonders, [F] wonders, [C] of [G] His [C] love.
{end_of_verse}
